          "case": "endpoints",
          "status": "not_applicable",
          "reason": "Statement of Hermite functions form a graph core for position multiplication: Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice [[def-countable-choice]]. Let $H=L^2(\\mathbb R,dx;\\mathbb C)$ with its first-variable-linear integral pairing, and let $Qf(x)=xf(x)$ on $D(Q)=\\{f\\in H:xf\\in H\\}$. Let $(g_n)_{n\\ge0}$ be the Hermite functions of [[thm-nrqm-oscillator-hermite-recurrence]]. Then $Q$ is self-adjoint on $D(Q)$, and the finite linear span of the $g_n$ is a core for $Q$: it is dense in $D(Q)$ for the graph norm $\\|f\\|_Q=(\\|f\\|_2^2+\\|Qf\\|_2^2)^{1/2}$. No additional closed-interval endpoint is quantified in this particular assertion. The given strict parameter inequalities and domain-qualified support/series identities are retained; this worksheet does not extend them across a forbidden endpoint."
        },
