          "reason": "Statement of Tensor products of sigma-finite L2 spaces: Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice [[def-countable-choice]]. Let $(X,\\mathcal A,\\mu)$ and $(Y,\\mathcal B,\\nu)$ be sigma-finite measure spaces, let $\\overline{\\mu\\times\\nu}$ be their completed product measure, and put $H_X=L^2(X,\\mu;\\mathbb C)$ and $H_Y=L^2(Y,\\nu;\\mathbb C)$ with the second-variable-linear pairing fixed in [[def-qft-fock-and-test-spaces]]. There is a unique unitary $$T:H_X\\widehat\\otimes H_Y\\longrightarrow L^2(X\\times Y,\\overline{\\mu\\times\\nu};\\mathbb C)$$ whose value on each elementary tensor is $T(f\\otimes g)(x,y)=f(x)g(y)$ almost everywhere. In particular, the Hilbert tensor completion is identified with the full product $L^2$ space, not only with the closure of a chosen class of product fu No additional closed-interval endpoint is quantified in this particular assertion. The given strict parameter inequalities and domain-qualified support/series identities are retained; this worksheet does not extend them across a forbidden endpoint."
