          "reason": "Statement of Bosonic and fermionic Fock operators with exact domains: Assume Countable Choice [[def-countable-choice]] and let $H$ be a separable complex Hilbert space with the second-variable-linear convention of [[def-qft-fock-and-test-spaces]]. On $\\mathcal D_{\\rm fin}$ define the bosonic creation and annihilation maps $a^\\dagger(h)$ and $a(h)$ and the fermionic maps $c^\\dagger(h)$ and $c(h)$ as in [[def-qft-fock-and-test-spaces]]. Write $a_n(h)$ and $a_n^\\dagger(h)$ for their restrictions to the $n$th bosonic sector. For bosons set $$D(a(h))=\\{\\Psi\\in\\mathcal F_s(H):\\sum_{n\\ge1}\\|a_n(h)\\Psi_n\\|^2<\\infty\\},\\qquad D(a^\\dagger(h))=\\{\\Psi\\in\\mathcal F_s(H):\\sum_{n\\ge0}\\|a_n^\\dagger(h)\\Psi_n\\|^2<\\infty\\}.$$ Then $\\mathcal F_s(H)$ and $\\mathcal F_a(H)$ are Hilbert spaces, $\\mathcal The forward iff axis adds no separately stated converse hypothesis here; the recorded claim is the displayed construction, identity, implication or scope qualification, not a characterization by a new necessary-and-sufficient condition."
