          "reason": "Statement of Second-quantized multipliers, joint spectrum and exact domains: Assume Countable Choice [[def-countable-choice]]. Let $(X,\\mathcal A,\\mu)$ be a sigma-finite measure space and let $\\boldsymbol\\omega=(\\omega_1,\\ldots,\\omega_d):X\\to\\mathbb R^d$ be a finite-valued measurable map, where $d\\ge1$. Put $H=L^2(X,\\mu;\\mathbb C)$ with the second-variable-linear pairing of [[def-qft-fock-and-test-spaces]], and form the bosonic Fock space $\\mathcal F_s(H)$. For $n\\ge1$, identify $H_s^{(n)}$ with the symmetric subspace of $L^2(X^n,\\overline{\\mu^{\\times n}};\\mathbb C)$ by iterating [[lem-qft-l2-product-tensor-identification]]. Set $X^0=\\{\\star\\}$, $s_0(\\star)=0$, and for $n\\ge1$ set $$s_n(x_1,\\ldots,x_n)=\\sum_{r=1}^n\\boldsymbol\\omega(x_r)\\in\\mathbb R^d.$$ For $1\\le j\\le d$, define $H_j$ b No additional closed-interval endpoint is quantified in this particular assertion. The given strict parameter inequalities and domain-qualified support/series identities are retained; this worksheet does not extend them across a forbidden endpoint."
        },
