          "claim": "By [F2], the annihilation-domain sum for $\\Psi$ is $\\sum_{n\\ge1}n/(n+1)^3\\le\\sum_{n\\ge1}n^{-2}$, and the creation-domain sum is $\\sum_{n\\ge0}(n+1)^{-2}$. Each is finite: the $k$th dyadic block of $\\sum_{n\\ge1}n^{-2}$ has at most $2^k$ terms each at most $2^{-2k}$, so its block sum is at most $2^{-k}$; the shifted series has the same convergence. Thus $\\Psi\\in D(a(e))\\cap D(a^\\dagger(e))$ while step 1.2 proves $\\Psi\\notin D(N)$. This is a domain distinction for the stated operators, not a physical or empirical claim.",
