          "status": "not_applicable",
          "reason": "Example of One-mode CCR/CAR and a vector outside the number-operator domain: Let $H=\\mathbb Ce$ with $\\|e\\|=1$, and write $|n\\rangle=e^{\\otimes n}$ for its normalized bosonic $n$-particle vector, including $|0\\rangle=\\Omega$. On the one-mode fermionic Fock space write $|1\\rangle=c^\\dagger(e)\\Omega$. The one-mode bosonic and fermionic operators satisfy the CCR and CAR on their stated domains. The bosonic number operator from [[lem-qft-second-quantized-spectrum]] is $N|n\\rangle=n|n\\rangle$ with $$D(N)=\\left\\{(c_n)_{n\\ge0}:\\sum_{n\\ge0}n^2|c_n|^2<\\infty\\right\\}.$$ The normalized Fock vector $$\\Psi=\\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty}(n+1)^{-3/2}|n\\rangle$$ belongs to $D(a(e))\\cap D(a^\\dagger(e))$ but not to $D(N)$. The displayed finite algebraic/test-contraction computation uses supplied objects rather than choosing elements of a family of nonempty sets; no nonempty-family selection is a separate conclusion."
